<PageTitle>Terms · @Brand.AppName</PageTitle>

<article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated @PrivacyPage.LastUpdated</p>

    <p>
        These terms are the agreement between you and @Brand.Operator ("we") for using @Brand.AppName, on the web and in
        its apps. By creating an account or using the app, you accept them. Our <a href="privacy">privacy policy</a>
        explains what we do with your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        @Brand.AppName is run by @(Brand.Operator)@(Brand.CompanyNumber is { } number ? $", {number}" : "")@(Brand.OperatorAddress is { } address ? $", of {address}" : "").
        @if (Brand.ContactEmail is { } contact)
        {
            <span> You can reach us at <a href="mailto:@contact">@contact</a>.</span>
        }
    </p>

    <h2>Using the app</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You may use @Brand.AppName for your own, personal, non-commercial use, for as long as you keep to these
            terms.</li>
        <li>The app itself (its software, design and name) belongs to us. Nothing here gives you rights in it beyond
            using it as it's offered.</li>
        <li>Don't try to get around rate limits, read other people's data, copy the catalog or our insights in bulk, or
            disrupt the service, including by automated means.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You need to be at least 13, or the age at which you can agree to this yourself where you live. If you're
            under 18, a parent or guardian must agree to these terms for you, and must be the one to buy a paid plan.</li>
        <li>Give an email address that is yours, and keep your sign-in details to yourself; you're responsible for what's
            done with your account. Tell us if you think someone else has used it.</li>
        <li>You can delete your account at any time in Settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you post</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Your comments, tips, insights and corrections stay yours. You let us store them and show them in the app, to
            other users, for as long as they're up; that permission ends when you delete them or your account.</li>
        <li>Only post what you have the right to post. Don't post anything unlawful, hateful, harassing, sexually
            explicit, or that infringes someone else's rights, and don't spam. Mark spoilers as spoilers.</li>
        <li>Posts are moderated. A post can be held for review (one with a link, for example), refused for blocked words,
            or hidden after other users flag it. When one of yours is hidden, you can still see it and why.</li>
        <li>
            If something in the app infringes your rights or is unlawful, flag it in the app
            @if (Brand.ContactEmail is { } report)
            {
                <span>or write to <a href="mailto:@report">@report</a></span>
            }
            saying what it is, where it is and why. We look at every report and take down what shouldn't be there.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The show information and insights</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Show and episode data comes from <CatalogCredits />@(Brand.Catalog.Licence switch
            {
                CatalogLicence.Own => ", under its own licence. Quotes and some facts come",
                CatalogLicence.Invented => ", which is invented. Quotes and some facts come",
                _ => ", and quotes and some facts"
            }) from Wikiquote and Wikidata, under the
            <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-SA</a> licence.
            Pictures belong to their owners.</li>
        <li>Insights, forecasts and recommendations are worked out from that data and can be wrong. They're
            for interest and planning, not promises: a forecast season may never come.</li>
        <li>"Where to watch" is worked out from what our data source says about a show's network and streaming
            service. It isn't a promise that the show is on that service in your country today; check with the
            service before you subscribe to it for a show.</li>
        <li>Links to streaming services take you to their sites, under their own terms. Some carry an affiliate code, so
            the service may pay us for a sign-up; that never changes what we show you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Plans and payments</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Browsing the catalog needs no account. With a free account, following, tracking, ratings, lists and the
            basic insights are free. Pro and Family add the insights
            listed on the plan page, which can change over time; we'll tell you before a paid feature you have is taken
            out of your plan.</li>
        <li>A paid plan is a subscription, by the month or the year, at the price shown when you buy it, taken by our
            payment provider. <strong>It renews automatically</strong> at the end of each period, at the price then
            current, until you cancel.</li>
        <li>You can cancel at any time on the plan page in Settings. You keep the plan until the end of the period
            you've paid for, and nothing more is charged.</li>
        <li><strong>Changing your mind:</strong> within 14 days of first buying a plan you can ask for all your money
            back, whatever the reason, by writing to us; the plan then ends. After that we don't refund part-periods,
            except where the law where you live gives you that right.</li>
        <li>If a payment fails, the payment provider may try again; if it still fails, the plan ends and your account
            goes back to the free plan. Nothing you made is lost.</li>
        <li>We may change prices; a new price applies from your next renewal, after we've told you at least 30 days
            ahead, and you can cancel before then.</li>
        <li>A Family plan's owner pays for up to five members, who get Pro while the owner's plan runs. When it ends,
            members go back to their own plans. What anyone made on a paid plan stays when the plan ends.</li>
        <li>If you bought a plan through an app store, the store takes the payment, and its rules on billing and
            refunds apply alongside these.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>We work to keep @Brand.AppName running and your data safe, and take backups, but we provide it as it is: we
            don't promise it will always be available or free of errors. We may change, add or remove features, and will
            tell you ahead of a change that takes away something you rely on.</li>
        <li>You're responsible for your device and your connection, and for keeping your own copy of anything you
            couldn't bear to lose: Settings → Export my data gives you one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Ending</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You can stop at any time by deleting your account, which also stops any subscription.</li>
        <li>We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms or puts the service or other people at risk. We'll
            tell you why, and give you the chance to put it right or to answer, unless the law or someone's safety
            prevents it. If we close an account for a reason that isn't a breach of these terms, we refund the unused
            part of any plan you've paid for.</li>
        <li>If we ever close the service, we'll give at least 30 days' notice, during which you can export your data,
            and refund the unused part of any paid plan.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we're responsible for</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>We're responsible for loss we cause that was a foreseeable result of our breaking these terms or failing to
            take reasonable care.</li>
        <li>As far as the law allows, we aren't responsible for indirect losses, for loss of profit or business (the
            app is for personal use), or for what other people post or what other services do; and our total
            responsibility to you is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months before the claim, or the price
